## Summary

I shipped a production-grade native **WinUI 3 / .NET 10** port of `ChargePlansWidget` at parity with the web source, committed as `c38dcbed2`.

**Capability check (per prompt):** WinUI 3 (Windows App SDK 1.6+) + .NET 10 + Fluent ΓÇö **present**. The solution builds clean and the full unit suite runs green, so this is **not** a BLOCKED-capability case.

**Implementation** (`apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/dashboard-widgets/ChargePlansWidget/`, 4-file pattern matching the codebase):
- **Model** ΓÇö `ChargePlan`/`RatePlanInfo` JSON parse adapters, active-plan selection (`active|scheduled ?? first`), statusΓåÆbadge mapping, the `planEntries.slice(2)` + `rateEntries` projection, currency/date/`%`/`kWh` formatting, and a **pure two-source merge** (`Combine`) reproducing the web `isLoading|isError|hasData|max(updatedAt)` flag combination.
- **Source** ΓÇö resolves the vehicle, runs **both** endpoints concurrently (`get_api_v1_charge_planner_history` + `_rate_plans`) and merges emissions via a channel; no HTTP in the view. Rate-plans run even with no vehicle (web parity).
- **ViewModel** ΓÇö `INotifyPropertyChanged` state holder, registry metadata (`charge-plans`, 2├ù4, 1├ù2ΓÇª4├ù40), PII-safe `view.opened` diagnostics.
- **View** ΓÇö every state renders: loading (skeleton), error (`TsQueryError` + retry), empty, stale/offline chips, plus compact target-SOC and standard (status badge, Target SOC/Departure `TsStatCard`s, plan details, Rate Plans section). Narrator names on every element; i18n via the facade (all 15 web keys already in en/ar/he).

